{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",
  "entry": ["scripts/*.mjs"],
  "project": [
    "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}!",
    "!src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}!",
    "!src/test/**!",
    // drums DR-02 kit-map. Excluded from PRODUCTION analysis only — that is what the
    // trailing `!` means here, exactly as it does on the two lines above, so the dev-mode
    // run still guards these files and knip stops offering to remove the line. Same shape
    // as the `ignore` entry below, one layer up: `docs/drums/ROADMAP.md` marks DR-02 `[~]`
    // — the core slice (note->pad table, CC4 hi-hat state machine, choke, debounce,
    // unmapped bucket, four vendor presets) merged, and the MIDI-learn wizard that builds
    // a `KitMapEngine` from a chosen preset is the app half, still pending. DELETE this
    // line when that wizard merges, or when any adapter constructs the engine for a live
    // e-kit — whichever is first. Dated, not permanent: if DR-02's app half is still
    // unbuilt when the next drums slice lands, the answer is to build it or to delete the
    // core layer, not to leave this here. (Roadmap T.27 is why it is written down at all.)
    "!src/core/drums/kitmap/**!",
    "scripts/**/*.mjs"
  ],
  "ignoreExportsUsedInFile": true,
  "rules": {
    "types": "off"
  },
  // Domain modules that are finished and tested but that no screen renders YET. Every entry names
  // the roadmap task that will wire it: when that task lands, DELETE the line — a permanent entry
  // here is how "green tests, never executed" hides. Nothing may be added without a task id.
  //
  // EMPTY, and that is the point: roadmap 4.9b (the lesson screen) was the last consumer owed, and
  // it landed. `core/curriculum/model.ts`, `content/curriculum/*` and `content/scores/demoScores.ts`
  // are now reachable from `src/main.tsx`, so knip's production mode guards them like everything
  // else. Do not add an entry here without a roadmap task id and a deletion condition.
  //
  // drums DR-04 model: finished + tested core layer whose production consumers are the
  // in-flight D0 slices (DR-02 kit-map engine emits its DrumHit, DR-05 engraves its
  // GrooveScore, DR-06 plays it). DELETE this line when the first drums screen that
  // renders or plays a groove merges (DR-05's gallery or DR-06's DrumsToday preview).
  // DR-02's kit-map layer above it is the same situation, handled in `project` instead —
  // see that line for why production-only exclusion is the sharper tool.
  "ignore": ["src/core/drums/model/**"]
}
